---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Sou-hardo/wifirank';
// Anyone whose contribution is approved and merged gets a line here.
const people = [
  {
    handle: 'jabir02',
    note: 'Raised the pain of picking an ISP after moving house, and listed the features that would have helped',
  },
  {
    handle: 'EhsanulHaqueSiam',
    note: 'Gave input that shaped the project',
  },
];
---
<Base title="Contributors"
  description="The people who shaped WifiRank. The code is open on GitHub and contributions are welcome; anything merged gets you a spot here.">
  <article class="wrap prose" style="padding-top:clamp(28px,5vw,56px);max-width:780px">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contributors</p>
    <h1>Built with a little help</h1>
    <p class="lede">WifiRank started because picking an internet provider in Dhaka is mostly guesswork and asking your cousin. It’s open source now, so if you can make it better, please do.</p>

    <h2 class="reveal"><span class="hl">Contributions are welcome</span></h2>
    <p>The code lives at <a href={REPO}>github.com/Sou-hardo/wifirank</a>. Open an issue, send a pull request, fix my typos. Any contribution that gets approved and merged shows up on this page, with your name on it. No pressure, but it’s a nicer reward than a GitHub star.</p>

    <h2 class="reveal"><span class="hl">The people</span></h2>
    <ul>
      {people.map((p) => (
        <li><a href={`https://github.com/${p.handle}`}><strong>@{p.handle}</strong></a>: {p.note}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>Your name could go here. Bro, it’s one pull request.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
